  "description": "T1\tBlack Walnut\t\r\n- Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 4-5m to create a tight and tidy shape. \r\n- Remove dead wood and crossing branches. \r\n\r\nNote:\r\nThe mature Black Walnut is approx. 18-22m tall and 12-16m wide. \r\nAfter the works are completed the tree will be approx. 16-18m tall and 10-14m wide.\r\n\r\nAll pruning cuts will adhere to BS 3998:2010.\r\n \r\nThe reason for the tree pruning is due to how severely the tree overhangs the surrounding property and roofs. This tree is very productive in producing large walnuts some in excess of 150g which have caused damage to surrounding properties.\r\n \r\nThe above works are as part of general maintenance to manage the tree in a healthy condition but at a slightly smaller size.",
